        how: "Separate the two tests that are currently one. stepTerrain rejects a move on the ground NORMAL alone, which is correct for a continuous slope and wrong for a lattice: between two integer samples one unit apart, bilinear interpolation puts the whole height difference into a band narrower than the step, so a one-unit stair reads as a cliff. The step-up path exists in physics/character/kinematic.js and is reachable there; what terrainWalk lacks is the check that asks whether a rejected move would be ACCEPTED one stepHeight higher.",
