        upstream: "*** A FIX WAS WRITTEN AND REMOVED, WHICH IS THE PART THAT MAKES THIS A ROUND RATHER THAN A PATCH. *** Re-probing the ground a fixed distance ahead keeps the frame-rate independence v4544 was built for -- a per-substep height-difference test shrinks with dt, so any wall becomes climbable at a high enough frame rate, and the normal-based limit exists to make the limit a property of the ground. But on a lattice the steep band between cells is WIDER THAN THE PROBE, so a probe short enough to be honest never clears it, and the 2.0-unit probe that finally does MOVED THE BODY 2.0 UNITS IN A STEP WHOSE BUDGET WAS 0.05. That is gains-ground-on-contact, the exact defect this session repaired in kinematic.js at v4544, and A TELEPORTING BOT IS WORSE THAN A STALLED ONE. So the round owes a test that distinguishes a lip from a cliff WITHOUT advancing the body to find out.",
