        how: "repalash/xatlas-three + repalash/xatlas.js (both MIT) -- a WASM/webworker compile of jpcy/xatlas (also MIT), the industry-standard chart-based UV parameterization library, wrapped for THREE.BufferGeometry with async unwrap() and packAtlas() calls. NOT gkjohnson's own work -- his copy is a fork; the actual authors are repalash (the three.js/WASM wrapper) and jpcy (the original C++ algorithm) -- correcting the attribution here so it is not mis-cited later. Only handles indexed geometry (BufferGeometryUtils.mergeVertices first for anything that isn't); interleaved geometry not yet supported.\n\nA second binding of the SAME underlying jpcy/xatlas found later, from a donmccurdy sweep: toji/watlas (MIT, appears in donmccurdy's own repos), a lower-level WASM wrapper that 'attempts to expose the native API as closely as possible... should be more flexible for a wider range of uses' than xatlas.js, and was written specifically to be used by donmccurdy's own gltf-transform SDK. Not a different technique -- worth knowing about if this tree ever adopts gltf-transform for broader asset-pipeline work, since then watlas would be the binding already wired for it rather than xatlas-three.",
